      "rect" : [
        39.663400000000003,
        470.35424999999998,
        312.03869999999995,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "been hijacked. He then called his mother, Louise Sweeney, told her the flight"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663400000000003,
        459.10384999999997,
        311.95260000000019,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "had been hijacked, and added that the passengers were thinking about storm-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664425000000001,
        447.85344999999995,
        282.32173999999998,
        9.4736250000000268
      ],
      "text" : "ing the cockpit to take control of the plane away from the hijackers.48"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        436.60505000000001,
        252.64712500000005,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "At 9:00, Lee Hanson received a second call from his son Peter:"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.659675000000007,
        414.10527500000001,
        276.0130249999998,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "It’s getting bad, Dad—A stewardess was stabbed—They seem to have"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        402.85487499999999,
        276.00482500000021,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "knives and Mace—They said they have a bomb—It’s getting very bad"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        391.60447499999998,
        276.0622249999999,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "on the plane—Passengers are throwing up and getting sick—The"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        380.35407499999997,
        276.06530000000032,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "plane is making jerky movements—I don’t think the pilot is flying the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        369.10367499999995,
        276.02327500000013,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "plane—I think we are going down—I think they intend to go to"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        357.85327499999994,
        276.00790000000006,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Chicago or someplace and fly into a building—Don’t worry, Dad—"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.660700000000006,
        346.60287499999993,
        209.73466499999995,
        9.474200000000053
      ],
      "text" : "If it happens, it’ll be very fast—My God, my God.49"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        324.10505000000001,
        299.99290000000013,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "The call ended abruptly.Lee Hanson had heard a woman scream just before"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        312.85464999999999,
        311.91160000000013,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "it cut off. He turned on a television, and in her home so did Louise Sweeney."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        301.60424999999998,
        256.41451499999994,
        9.4728250000000003
      ],
      "text" : "Both then saw the second aircraft hit the World Trade Center.50"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        290.35505000000001,
        300.02877500000005,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "At 9:03:11,United Airlines Flight 175 struck the South Tower of the World"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        279.10464999999999,
        312.03072500000007,
        9.472424999999987
      ],
      "text" : "Trade Center.51 All on board, along with an unknown number of people in"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659525000000002,
        267.85464999999999,
        125.30317500000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "the tower, were killed instantly."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659525000000002,
        245.41637500000002,
        140.14927499999999,
        9.2147500000000093
      ],
      "text" : "The Hijacking of American 77"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659525000000002,
        234.10447500000001,
        312.06432500000005,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "American Airlines Flight 77 was scheduled to depart from Washington Dulles"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661574999999999,
        222.85407499999999,
        312.0356250000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "for Los Angeles at 8:10. The aircraft was a Boeing 757 piloted by Captain"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662599999999998,
        211.60367499999998,
        312.03664999999995,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Charles F. Burlingame and First Officer David Charlebois. There were four"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662599999999998,
        200.35327499999997,
        280.88616500000001,
        9.4738000000000397
      ],
      "text" : "flight attendants. On September 11, the flight carried 58 passengers.52"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        189.10505000000001,
        300.02160000000021,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "American 77 pushed back from its gate at 8:09 and took off at 8:20.At 8:46,"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        177.85464999999999,
        312.03665000000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "the flight reached its assigned cruising altitude of 35,000 feet. Cabin service"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        166.60424999999998,
        312.01922500000029,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "would have begun.At 8:51,American 77 transmitted its last routine radio com-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        155.35384999999997,
        312.064325,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "munication.The hijacking began between 8:51 and 8:54.As on American 11"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        144.10344999999995,
        312.0438249999998,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "and United 175, the hijackers used knives (reported by one passenger) and"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        132.85304999999994,
        312.03665000000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "moved all the passengers (and possibly crew) to the rear of the aircraft (reported"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662374999999997,
        121.60264999999994,
        312.0335750000001,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "by one flight attendant and one passenger).Unlike the earlier flights,the Flight"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662374999999997,
        110.35224999999994,
        312.02537499999994,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "77 hijackers were reported by a passenger to have box cutters. Finally, a pas-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664424999999994,
        99.101849999999942,
        311.89007500000014,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "senger reported that an announcement had been made by the “pilot” that the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664424999999994,
        87.851449999999943,
        312.01205000000004,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "plane had been hijacked.Neither of the firsthand accounts mentioned any stab-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664425000000023,
        76.601049999999944,
        311.99257499999999,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "bings or the threat or use of either a bomb or Mace,though both witnesses began"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664425000000023,
        65.350649999999945,
        131.93444,
        9.4764250000000629
      ],
      "text" : "the flight in the first-class cabin.53"
    }
  ],
